Chapter: Record Cycle
  cites Codex chapter General
  cites Codex chapter Text

 Probe: a derived Show on a recursive variant traverses a deep chain
 without crashing. build-chain is tail-recursive, so constructing the
 chain does not blow the stack; the derived `__show_Chain` then walks
 the whole structure. The test only asserts the result is non-empty.

Section: Types

  Chain =
    | Cons (Integer) (Chain)
    | Nil
    deriving Show

Section: Build

  build-chain : Integer, Chain -> Chain
  build-chain (n) (acc) =
    if n <= 0 then acc
    else build-chain (n - 1) (Cons n acc)

Section: Entry Point

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let root = build-chain 100 Nil in
      print-line-uni (if text-length (show root) > 0 then "ok" else "empty")
  end

